---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import historiaImg from '../../assets/images/historia.webp';
import { ORIGIN_LINE } from '../../config/eu';
---

<section id="story" class="bg-terracota-300 py-24 md:py-32">
  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-site items-center gap-12 px-6 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-16 md:px-10">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow reveal mb-4">The story</p>
      <h2 class="h-display reveal text-4xl text-carbon md:text-5xl">
        Ten years leading<br />by example
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-[1.05rem] leading-relaxed text-slate-800">
        <p class="reveal">
          Selva Brava starts from a simple question: why do we accept what we accept?
          Why do we put things on our skin we'd never choose to put in our bodies?
          Out of that question — and a lot of mountain, sea and common sense — came
          what we are.
        </p>
        <p class="reveal reveal-delay-1">
          We've been making mineral sunscreen for ten years. No synthetic filters.
          No plastic packaging. No promises we can't back with evidence.
        </p>
        <p class="reveal reveal-delay-2">
          {ORIGIN_LINE}. Natural cosmetics are our first ground for expression: where
          we put into practice what we believe. Small-batch production, ingredients you
          can read and understand, and a product built for real conditions — altitude,
          snow, salt, long exposure.
        </p>
        <p class="reveal reveal-delay-2">
          We don't chase trends. We believe a company is defined as much by what it
          refuses as by what it creates. And we choose to create on our own judgement.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <figure class="reveal reveal-delay-1">
      <Image
        src={historiaImg}
        alt="Turmeric, cacao, shea butter and herbs on raw linen"
        class="w-full rounded-sm object-cover"
        widths={[600, 1200]}
        sizes="(min-width: 768px) 50vw, 100vw"
      />
      <figcaption class="eyebrow mt-3 !text-slate-400">
        Turmeric, cacao, shea — the raw material, as it is
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>
